// PENDING: a transition guard whose operands are integers of DIFFERENT
// carriers retains no Guard fact, so the entry's Unit plan is omitted at
// `state graph: terminator: conditional successors: guard expression`.
//
// The only load-bearing token is `i`'s type. With `i: u64` — the same
// carrier the length has — this program checks. With `i: i32` it is refused
// with the downstream symptom, "selected ProgramEntry establishment rejoins
// 0 Terminal attachment identities".
//
// The spec settled this. `wiki/spec/language/numeric_values.md` says builtin
// fixed-integer comparisons "require no common operand carrier, implicit
// cast, or representability of either value in the other operand's carrier",
// and that "Terminal normalization and target realization implement it;
// neither may substitute an unsigned promotion or reject source operands
// merely because their integer carriers differ". `af32a85a4e4` closed that
// owner question as a documentation checkpoint carrying "No compiler
// behavior changes", so the implementation is owed.
//
// The site is `construct_integer_comparison` in
// `omega-rust/psi/pipeline/04_typed-trees-to-checked-trees/src/values/scalar/boolean_lowering.rs`:
//
//     if !is_integer(left_type) || scalar_expression_type(&right)? != left_type {
//         return None;
//     }
//
// The checked representation is not what blocks it —
// `CheckedBooleanExpression::IntegerComparison` holds two independent scalar
// expressions and never required them to agree. Note the spec's other
// sentence when repairing it: "Source-independent verification retains the
// exact operand subjects, carriers, relation and polarity", so rewriting the
// comparison into a sign test over same-carrier compares is not the shape;
// the mixed comparison should survive as itself.
//
// Three samples wait on this: `cli/text/{parse_int,roman_numeral,string_hash}`
// all walk a text carrier with an `i32` index against its `u64` length.
// Promote this to `pass/expressions/` with an exit when it lands.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    text: [u8; 8];
    i: i32;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console {
    self.i = 0;
    transition { _ -> step() }

    state step(&mut self) {
        transition self.i < self.text.len {
            true -> guarded()
            _ -> done()
        }
    }

    // The re-guard keeps the increment's own overflow obligation out of the
    // way, exactly as `cli/text/parse_int` does, so the guard comparison is
    // the only thing this fixture pins.
    state guarded(&mut self) {
        transition self.i >= 0 && self.i < 8 {
            true -> bump()
            _ -> done()
        }
    }

    state bump(&mut self) {
        self.i = self.i + 1;
        transition { _ -> step() }
    }

    state done(&mut self) { self.console.exit_process(0); }
}
